    "check": "fifteen councillors returned unopposed for fifteen seats; the nominations are in the Belfast News-Letter, 5 May 1949, p. 3 (citation confirmed 7 Nov 2026 from the page images) ('... T. W. F. Bryson, ... and C. D. Whaley (councillors). The Nationalists nominated for the North Ward were Messrs. C. M'Keown and John Nethercott (aldermen); J. Gormley, H. Morris, Leo Quinn, M. Kelly, and P. J. O'Hare'); names as printed in the Fermanagh Herald, 28 May 1949, p. 5",
