  "note": "Election of the new Enniskillen Borough Council in 1949; the fifteen councillors were returned unopposed on 4 May. The aldermen are filed separately (enniskillen-borough-council-aldermen). The fifteen councillors were returned unopposed: Quinn, Morris, O'Hare, Kelly and Gormley for the North Ward (Anti-Partitionists), and ten Unionists for the East and South Wards, whose nominations are printed together without a ward breakdown, so the borough is recorded as one area. The aldermen, with the North Ward aldermanic poll, are filed separately (enniskillen-borough-council-aldermen). Returned unopposed."
